Subject: [PATCH] Xcode: avoid ApplicationServices headers with GCC

The ApplicationServices umbrella header includes CoreGraphics and
ImageIO declarations using Apple's Blocks extension, which GCC does
not support.

CMake only uses this header to open generated Xcode projects through
Launch Services. Disable that optional operation for GCC builds while
retaining the Xcode project generator and normal Clang behavior.

Upstream-Status: Pending

diff --git a/Source/cmGlobalXCodeGenerator.cxx b/Source/cmGlobalXCodeGenerator.cxx
--- a/Source/cmGlobalXCodeGenerator.cxx
+++ b/Source/cmGlobalXCodeGenerator.cxx
@@ -59,7 +59,7 @@
 #  include <CoreFoundation/CFString.h>
 #  include <CoreFoundation/CFURL.h>
 #  include <CoreFoundation/CFUUID.h>
-#  if !TARGET_OS_IPHONE
+#  if !TARGET_OS_IPHONE && defined(__clang__)
 #    define HAVE_APPLICATION_SERVICES
 #    include <ApplicationServices/ApplicationServices.h>
 #  endif
